---
description: Keep Cursor fast and token-efficient
alwaysApply: true
---

- Be concise and execution-focused.
- Do not re-read large files repeatedly.
- Read only the files needed for the current task.
- Prefer targeted search over broad scans.
- Do not propose large rewrites when a local patch works.
- Do not invoke extra tools, agents, or scans unless they materially help the task.
- Summaries should contain only actionable points, not long theory.
